<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>BTA Customer Bus Operations</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css" />
  </head>
  <body class="workspace-page">
    <main class="workspace-shell">
      <section class="hero-band">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Fleet Visibility</p>
          <h1>Buses Currently In Operation</h1>
          <p class="subtitle">
            Search active buses by route and stop coverage, then compare the rendered fleet results
            with the lookup event that Graylog receives. If an admin has armed GPS spoofing for one
            of the returned buses, the rendered location fields below will show the spoofed view.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <nav class="page-nav">
            <a class="nav-link" href="/customer/dashboard">Customer Dashboard</a>
            <a class="nav-link" href="/customer/book-ticket">Book Ticket</a>
            <a class="nav-link active" href="/customer/buses">Buses In Operation</a>
            <a class="nav-link" href="/customer/ticket-status">Ticket Status</a>
          </nav>
          <form method="post" action="/logout">
            <button class="secondary" type="submit">Log Out</button>
          </form>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="detail-layout">
        <article class="detail-card detail-card-wide">
          <div class="card-topline">
            <p class="eyebrow">Bus Search</p>
            <span class="status-pill neutral">GET /api/customer/buses</span>
          </div>
          <h2>Route And Fleet Filters</h2>
          <p class="section-copy">
            The lookup emits `customer_bus_lookup` with the route, stop, vehicle-status, and
            operator-label values selected below. Armed GPS scenarios are applied to the matching
            bus at render time so the customer page and Graylog both reflect the same integrity
            issue.
          </p>

          <form
            class="detail-form"
            method="get"
            action="/api/customer/buses"
            data-console-form="buses"
          >
            <div class="form-grid">
              <label>
                <span>Route Name Contains</span>
                <input type="text" name="route_name" value="Majestic" />
              </label>
              <label>
                <span>Origin Stop</span>
                <input type="text" name="origin_stop" value="Majestic" />
              </label>
              <label>
                <span>Destination Stop</span>
                <input type="text" name="destination_stop" value="Whitefield" />
              </label>
              <label>
                <span>Vehicle Status</span>
                <select name="vehicle_status">
                  <option value="all">All</option>
                  <option value="in_service">In Service</option>
                  <option value="boarding">Boarding</option>
                  <option value="layover">Layover</option>
                </select>
              </label>
              <label>
                <span>Result Limit</span>
                <input type="number" name="limit" min="1" max="100" value="12" />
              </label>
              <label>
                <span>Operator Label</span>
                <input type="text" name="operator_label" value="customer-bus-refresh" />
              </label>
            </div>
            <div class="form-actions">
              <button type="submit">Fetch Buses</button>
              <a class="ghost-link" href="/customer/dashboard">Back To Dashboard</a>
            </div>
          </form>
        </article>

        <article class="detail-card">
          <div class="card-topline">
            <p class="eyebrow">Graylog Signals</p>
            <span class="status-pill success">Structured JSON</span>
          </div>
          <h2>Expected Events</h2>
          <ul class="detail-list">
            <li>`customer_bus_lookup` with route and stop filters.</li>
            <li>`http_access` showing the exact bus-query string.</li>
            <li>Matching armed buses also emit `gps_signal_anomaly` and `ghost_bus_projection`.</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="chip-wrap">
            <span class="data-chip">message:customer_bus_lookup</span>
            <span class="data-chip">vehicle_status_filter</span>
            <span class="data-chip">route_name_filter</span>
            <span class="data-chip">message:gps_signal_anomaly</span>
            <span class="data-chip">message:ghost_bus_projection</span>
          </div>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section class="detail-layout">
        <article class="detail-card detail-card-wide">
          <div class="card-topline">
            <p class="eyebrow">Fleet Results</p>
            <span class="status-pill neutral">Rendered Response</span>
          </div>
          <div id="buses-summary" class="result-empty">
            Run a bus lookup to render active fleet entries and summary metrics.
          </div>
          <div class="table-wrap">
            <table class="results-table">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>Bus</th>
                  <th>Route</th>
                  <th>Displayed Location</th>
                  <th>Expected Location</th>
                  <th>Spoofed Location</th>
                  <th>Displayed Stop</th>
                  <th>Destination</th>
                  <th>Integrity</th>
                  <th>Schedule Delta</th>
                  <th>Status</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody id="buses-table-body">
                <tr>
                  <td colspan="10" class="table-placeholder">No buses loaded yet.</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="detail-card">
          <div class="card-topline">
            <p class="eyebrow">Raw API Body</p>
            <span class="status-pill neutral">JSON</span>
          </div>
          <pre id="console-response" class="response-pre">Run the console to inspect the response body.</pre>
        </article>
      </section>
    </main>
    <script src="/console.js"></script>
  </body>
</html>
